WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:03.280
I was born in Uganda in 1950,

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:07.520
and a year and a half later
I slipped out of bed one day

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:09.400
and I collapsed on the floor.

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:12.880
My parents immediately thought,
"Oh, it's polio".

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:19.080
It would be hard to imagine what a
world without vaccines would be like.

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:20.600
It would really be quite horrible.

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:24.680
There would be outbreaks of disease
regularly, all over the world.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.760
The true deep impact,
and the global impact, of vaccines

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:35.400
just can't be overestimated.

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:45.120
My grandmother, she used to tell a
story

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:48.800
about when they would hear the
bells on a hearse

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:51.080
going down the
high street, a funeral.

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:54.680
She said as children they would
rush to their nursery window

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:57.080
to see if there were
white ribbons on the horses

00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:59.120
which meant it was a child funeral,

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.640
and they happened
several times a week.

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:12.040
It typically affected children.

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:16.440
One of the names for polio
was infantile paralysis.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:47.840
It's quite difficult to imagine
a world without vaccines.

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:50.000
Life expectancy would be a lot lower.

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:52.040
People would have to lock
themselves away

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:54.760
and only come out again
when it was safe.

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:56.200
And ironically,

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:57.600
there would be such a demand

00:01:57.680 --> 00:01:59.000
to do something that vaccines

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:00.640
would inevitably emerge.

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:08.760
Vaccines are likely the most
important public health intervention

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:10.520
of the last 100 years.

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:12.680
They've saved over a billion lives.

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:19.480
With the roll out of vaccines

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:22.800
we have seen a massive reduction
in child mortality

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:24.440
in sub-Saharan Africa.

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:31.320
I am born in the Gambia

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:34.200
and growing up there
I lost a brother to measles.

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:37.000
To lose somebody
at a very premature age

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:41.560
from a disease preventable by
vaccines is absolutely devastating.

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:54.560
Vaccines can prevent cancer
and there are two cancer vaccines.

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:04.200
With the roll out of the current
malaria vaccine

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:08.240
we are expecting to see a reduction
of 40% of malaria deaths.

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:17.440
You could bring a vaccine to people

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:18.640
but will they take it?

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:23.640
Anti-vaccination fears have been
around for over a century.

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:28.320
We know from the 1850s, when Jenner
first developed smallpox vaccine

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:29.960
there were actually
quite a few protests.

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:33.920
A lot of it was about civil
rights and libertarian values.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:36.800
There were arguments saying
that it was poisonous,

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:39.760
that children who received
a smallpox vaccine

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:43.120
would develop bovine
or cow-like traits.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:45.960
A lot of it was just a genuine
knowledge void

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:49.640
that a lot of people had in the 1850s
that they still have today.

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:55.280
On the one hand we have the really
hardcore anti-vaccination groups,

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:58.640
but a lot of people are actually
in the middle,

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:00.760
and I think what we need to do
is just engage with people

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.560
where they are
and where they are talking

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:05.080
and not discount their real concerns.

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:08.480
People want to understand things,
they want to be confident,

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:09.840
they might be afraid of needles.

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:12.680
We have to understand their context
and where they're coming from

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:15.840
and what are their past experiences
with health and vaccines.

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:19.880
We have to ensure that people
understand it and they will take it.

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:33.040
A world without vaccines, it would
be a matter of economic status

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:37.280
where the children of the wealthy
will have access to healthcare

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:38.480
will be surviving.

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:42.760
Vaccines are the only public health
intervention that can bring equality.

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:45.320
So women don't need
to have five, 10 children

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:47.640
just to see three of them
grow to old age.

00:04:48.920 --> 00:04:52.000
This isn't about
just individual rights,

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:55.000
when you take a vaccine
it's protecting yourself,

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:58.080
it's protecting your family,
and it's protecting your community.

00:04:58.160 --> 00:04:59.320
It's not just a personal choice,

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.360
it's a moral choice as well
that affects other people.

00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:08.960
It's impossible to emphasise
how important vaccines are.

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:12.120
And the reason that we don't often
realise that they're important

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:14.640
is that we've eradicated
many of these diseases.

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:19.040
The idea that vaccines could be
a victim of their own success,

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:21.560
it's about taking things
for granted, isn't it?

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:23.680
And not looking behind

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:26.880
what the privileges we have
in the modern world are,

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:28.440
and what makes it the modern world,

00:05:28.520 --> 00:05:31.640
and makes it a safe place
for most of us to be,

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:35.800
and vaccines are absolutely
at the heart of that.

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:37.280
They're fundamental.

